The file crates/functor-symbols/data/glyphs.tsv contains glyph outlines from
@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font 4.1.3 (https://github.com/mathjax/MathJax-fonts),
which is under the Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
The outlines come from the New Computer Modern fonts by Antonis Tsolomitis,
which are under the GUST Font License.

scripts/extract-glyphs.mjs makes this file. The script changes the format of the
data only: it adds a move command at the start of each path and writes one glyph
on each line.

The files web/src/fonts/functor-lm-*.woff2 and crates/functor-paper/data/fonts/functor-lm-*.otf
are subsets of Latin Modern Roman 10 (regular, italic, bold, bold italic) and Latin Modern Mono 10 by B. Jackowski and J. M. Nowacki, under the
GUST Font License (web/src/fonts/GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt). They hold Latin letters
and punctuation only, some are converted to WOFF2, and all have new file names. The fonts
are not otherwise changed.
